# CLAUDE.md - Dayless.ai Development Guide

This file defines how to build and maintain the Dayless.ai project. Follow these rules exactly. Do not deviate unless explicitly asked.

## ENVIRONMENT

- Framework: Next.js 16 with App Router (MANDATORY)
- Language: TypeScript 5 (strict)
- Runtime: bun (not npm, not yarn)
- Database: Prisma ORM + SQLite (file at prisma/dev.db via `DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"`)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS 4 + shadcn/ui (New York style)
- State: Zustand (client) + TanStack Query (server)
- Auth: NextAuth.js v4 (Credentials provider)
- Animations: Framer Motion
- Icons: Lucide React
- AI: z-ai-web-dev-sdk (backend ONLY)
- Realtime: Socket.io mini-services

## Critical Rules

- Port: ONLY 3000. Never use other ports in Next.js.
- Single route: ALL UI is in `src/app/page.tsx` - a client component that switches views. Do NOT create new routes.
- API routes: Use `/api/` routes, NOT server actions.
- Gateway: External requests use XTransformPort query param. NEVER hardcode ports in URLs.
- Dev server: Runs via `bun run dev`. Do NOT kill it or delete `.next` manually.
- Database changes: Run `bun run db:push` (not migrations in dev).
- AI SDK: `z-ai-web-dev-sdk` MUST be used in backend ONLY. Never import it in client components.
- Preview: NEVER tell user to visit localhost:3000. Use "Preview Panel" instead.

