## Prisma Client Cache Warning

IMPORTANT: When adding NEW models to `schema.prisma` after the dev server has already started, the cached Prisma client in `globalThis` will NOT include the new model. This causes `db.newModel` to be undefined.

Solutions (pick one):

1. Restart the dev server after schema changes
2. Use raw SQL: `db.$queryRawUnsafe('SELECT * FROM "NewTable"')`
3. Create fresh PrismaClient per call: `const prisma = new PrismaClient()`

## AI CHAT PATTERN (core feature)

The AI chat is the central feature. The flow in `/api/chat/route.ts`:

1. Receive user message (`teamId`, `senderId`, `senderName`, `content`)
2. Save user message to DB
3. Build context by gathering:
   - Current team info + member list
   - Relevant Knowledge Base entries
   - Open GitHub Issues from connected projects
   - Open Jira Issues from connected projects
   - Recent chat history (last 20 messages)
4. Construct system prompt with:
   - Role definition (Scrum Master persona)
   - Team context (members, projects)
   - Knowledge base
   - Issue summaries from GitHub/Jira
   - Instructions for special actions
5. Call LLM via `z-ai-web-dev-sdk`
6. Parse AI response for special actions:
   - `[GITHUB_ACTION: create_issue | repo: ... | title: ...]`
   - `[JIRA_ACTION: create_issue | project: ... | summary: ...]`
   - Knowledge Entry auto-extraction
7. Execute actions (create issues, update status, etc.)
8. Save AI response to DB
9. Return both user message and AI message

## AUTHENTICATION PATTERN

- NextAuth v4 Credentials provider
- JWT sessions (30-day maxAge)
- Auto-register: if user doesn't exist, create on first login (password >= 6 chars)
- Use raw SQL for User model access to avoid Prisma cache issues
- AuthGate component wraps the entire app
- `useSession()` hook for session detection (NOT manual fetch)
- Logout: `window.location.href = '/'` (full reload, NOT `router.refresh`)

## LANDING PAGE PATTERN

When building a landing page:

- Create as a standalone component, NOT inside the app router
- Full-width sections with `min-h-screen` or `py-20 md:py-32`
- Hero: Large heading (`text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold`), subtitle, CTA buttons
- Feature grid: 3-column on desktop, 1-column on mobile
- Social proof: logos, testimonials, stats
- Use `bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 via-white to-[accent]-50/30` for subtle gradients
- Decorative blobs: absolute rounded-full `bg-[accent]-100/40 blur-3xl` positioned off-screen
- CTA sections with emerald accent buttons
- Smooth scroll between sections
- Framer Motion fade-in animations on scroll (use IntersectionObserver or whileInView)

## COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID

- DO NOT create new routes in `app/` directory - everything goes in `page.tsx`
- DO NOT import `z-ai-web-dev-sdk` in client components
- DO NOT hardcode ports in URLs - use `XTransformPort` query param
- DO NOT use `router.refresh()` for auth state changes - use `window.location.href`
- DO NOT delete `.next` while the dev server is running
- DO NOT use indigo/blue as primary colors
- DO NOT build custom UI components when shadcn/ui has them
- DO NOT skip responsive design - mobile-first always
- DO NOT forget sticky footer with `min-h-screen flex flex-col + mt-auto`
- DO NOT use `useState` for side effects - use `useEffect`

## GIT CONVENTIONS

- Commit messages in English, imperative mood: "Add GitHub Issues integration"
- Feature branches: `feature/github-integration`
- One logical change per commit

## TESTING

- Do NOT write test files
- Manual testing via Preview Panel
- Use `bun run lint` to check code quality before delivering
- Verify all API endpoints return `{ success: true, data: ... }` format
